UPDATE tools SET description = $x$AI voice platform built around a studio-style voiceover editor (200+ voices, 30+ languages and accents) for e-learning, explainer videos, and presentations, alongside a separate conversational voice-agent product and a low-latency text-to-speech API (Falcon).$x$
 WHERE slug = 'murf-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Murf is an AI voice platform that has expanded well beyond its original voiceover-editor product. The company now organizes itself around four offerings: Murf Agents (inbound/outbound conversational voice agents), the Murf API (built on its own Falcon TTS model, marketed for sub-100ms time-to-first-audio), Murf Studio (the classic voiceover editor most users know it for), and Dub. Murf's own homepage now leads with the agents and API products rather than the Studio editor.

Studio remains a text-to-speech and voiceover production tool aimed at e-learning, explainer videos, corporate presentations, and marketing content. It includes a built-in editor that syncs audio with video and slides, timing controls, word-level emphasis, and style controls (conversational, professional, excited), plus pitch and speed adjustment. Murf states Studio offers 200+ AI voices across 30+ languages and accents; separately, the Murf API page states 150+ voices in 35+ languages and styles — these are Murf's own, differing figures for two different products, not one combined number.

On the API side, Murf offers pay-as-you-go pricing: roughly $0.01 per 1,000 characters for Falcon-based conversational TTS (under 100ms time-to-first-audio), $0.03 per 1,000 characters for studio-quality TTS, $0.10 per minute for a voice-changer feature, and $0.02 per 1,000 characters for translation, with an API free trial that includes $10 of credit every month and no credit card required.

Studio pricing has four tiers. Studio Free is $0/month, with 10 projects and 10 minutes of voice generation per month, one editor seat, no downloads, and no commercial rights. Studio Creator is listed at $19/month, billed annually at $228/year, and includes 100 projects, an annual pool of 24 hours of voice generation, all 200+ voices, unlimited downloads, and commercial rights. Studio Business is listed at $66/month, billed annually at $792/year, and includes 500 projects, an annual pool of 96 hours of voice generation, priority support, and a business license, but does not include voice cloning or team collaboration — the max editor seats is 1. Studio Enterprise is custom-priced and includes unlimited voice generation, SSO, AI translation, and custom voice cloning as an add-on. The month-to-month-only rate for Creator and Business (without annual billing) is not published on Murf's pricing page and is not stated here.

Limitations: the free Studio plan's lack of downloads and commercial rights makes it usable only for testing, not production. Creator and Business voice-generation allowances are annual pools (24 and 96 hours per year respectively), which require pacing across the year rather than a simple monthly budget. Voice cloning is not available on Business — it is an Enterprise add-on. The platform's homepage now foregrounds conversational agents and the API over the Studio editor, so buyers evaluating it purely as a voiceover tool should confirm Studio is still the right fit for their workflow.

Studio suits instructional designers, e-learning content creators, marketing teams, and video creators who need professional voiceovers without hiring voice talent. The Murf API and Agents products suit developers and businesses building real-time voice applications or automated calling agents.$x$
