UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Replit Agent 4 runs parallel agents that build authentication, database, backend, and frontend components simultaneously, and includes a Security Agent that scans codebases for vulnerabilities.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'replit' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Replit is a browser-based development platform that combines a cloud IDE, AI coding agent, and instant deployment into a single environment. No local setup is required — users write, run, and ship code entirely in the browser, making it accessible for beginners and fast for prototyping.

The current generation, Agent 4, repositions Replit from an AI coding agent toward a broader creative agent, described by Replit as turning ideas into apps, designs, slides, and more, with design variants generated on an infinite canvas as a headline feature.

Agent 4 introduces multi-task parallelism: instead of building an app sequentially, it spins up parallel agents that handle authentication, database setup, backend logic, and frontend code at the same time, with progress visible in a dedicated panel. The Security Agent performs codebase scanning at three levels: a free dependency and static code analysis pass, a white-box scan, and a combined white-box plus black-box scan; Replit has not published scan duration figures.

Pricing, read from replit.com/pricing, has no listed $0 account tier. Core costs $20/month billed monthly, or $18/month billed annually, and includes $20 in monthly credits plus a Free Mode allowance of up to 30 hours of chat and 60 projects. Pro costs $100/month billed monthly, or $90/month billed annually, includes $100 in credits, 10 parallel agents, up to 15 collaborators and 50 viewers, and 28-day database rollback. Enterprise pricing is custom and adds SSO/SAML, single-tenant environments, and static outbound IPs.

Free Mode, included inside the paid tiers, resets its usage allowance every 5 hours and always uses automatic intelligent model routing rather than manual model selection, which is reserved for Power/Max modes. Generated code across all tiers often needs review before production use, and the browser-based environment can feel slower than local editors for large projects.

Replit suits developers who want to go from idea to deployed app quickly, students learning full-stack development, and small teams that need built-in collaboration and automated security scanning without managing their own infrastructure, provided they are willing to pay for a Core or Pro plan since no free account tier is currently offered.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'replit' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET pros = ARRAY[$x$Agent 4 runs parallel agents for auth, database, backend, and frontend simultaneously$x$, $x$Security Agent offers three scan levels, including a free dependency and static analysis pass$x$, $x$Zero local setup — write, run, and deploy entirely in the browser$x$, $x$Pro plan supports up to 15 collaborators and 50 viewers with 28-day database rollback$x$, $x$Annual billing gives roughly a 10% discount on both Core and Pro plans$x$]::text[]
 WHERE slug = 'replit' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET cons = ARRAY[$x$No published free account tier — Free Mode is a usage mode inside paid plans, not a standalone free plan$x$, $x$Free Mode usage resets every 5 hours and only supports automatic model routing, not manual model choice$x$, $x$Pro plan at $100/month billed monthly is expensive for solo developers who don't exhaust their credits$x$, $x$Browser-based environment is slower for large projects than local editors like Cursor or Zed$x$, $x$Generated code often requires review and cleanup before production deployment$x$]::text[]
 WHERE slug = 'replit' AND lang = 'en';

