UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Adaptive math learning platform (Synthesis Tutor) originally built for SpaceX employees' children, now open to the public. Covers K-5 math ages 5-11 through game-based challenges; a separate product, Synthesis Teams, covers ages 8-14.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'synthesis' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Synthesis is an AI-powered math and problem-solving platform that originated in 2014 when founder Josh Dahn was asked by Elon Musk to launch an experimental school for SpaceX employees' children. It was initially available only to SpaceX families before expanding into a public product suite.

Today Synthesis ships two separate products: Synthesis Tutor, an adaptive K-5 math program for ages 5-11, and Synthesis Teams, a game-based program for ages 8-14 focused on problem-solving, leadership, and critical thinking. Pricing for Synthesis Teams was not available on the vendor's pricing page at the time of review.

Synthesis Tutor presents math as puzzles and strategic challenges rather than drill-and-practice, with an AI that tracks each child's understanding and adjusts difficulty and topic focus. It also includes progress tracking for parents. The company additionally offers free adaptive multiplication flashcards outside of any paid subscription.

Synthesis Tutor is sold across two plan families — Individual (covers 1 child) and Family (covers up to 7 children per the vendor's homepage, though its pricing page separately lists Family Lifetime as covering up to 10) — and three billing modes: monthly, annual, and one-time lifetime purchase. On the most recent check, sale pricing was Individual Monthly $35/month, Individual Annual $300/year, Individual Lifetime $999 one-time, Family Monthly $29/month, Family Annual $119/year, and Family Lifetime $1,499 one-time. The vendor's homepage and pricing page disagree on the non-sale 'regular' rates, so those figures are omitted here. A 7-day free trial is available on monthly and annual subscriptions but not on Lifetime purchases; there is no ongoing free plan.

Synthesis Tutor covers only K-5 math (ages 5-11); broader problem-solving skills for ages 8-14 require the separate Synthesis Teams product. The game-based approach may not satisfy parents seeking traditional curriculum alignment or standardized test preparation, and children who prefer direct instruction may find the exploratory format frustrating. The vendor's own pricing pages also contain internal inconsistencies on regular rates and child counts, making exact cost comparisons difficult.

Best suited for parents of elementary-age children (5-11) who want an engaging, adaptive supplement to school math, particularly larger families that benefit from the Family plan's multi-child coverage.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'synthesis' AND lang = 'en';

